Data
  The loss trace in docs/traces/ (LEO_downlink_loss-Ger0804-170001-1h.npz) is
  a Starlink downlink loss trace derived from the LENS dataset
  (https://github.com/clarkzjw/LENS) by the authors of:
    T. Wang, T. Liu, Y. Li, J. Zhao, R. Gao, S. Wu and J. Pan, "Packet Loss
    Modeling and Forward Erasure Correction for LEO Satellite Networks",
    IEEE Transactions on Communications, 2026.
  It was provided to us by T. Liu as a text file, one per-packet outcome per
  line (1 = lost, 0 = received), and is published here with the authors'
  permission. We only converted it to the NumPy .npz format, to compress it and
  to match the input format of the simulator; the sequence of outcomes is
  unchanged.
  Like the LENS dataset, the trace is distributed under Creative Commons
  Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/. 
  If you use it, please cite
  the paper above and the LENS dataset (J. Zhao and J. Pan, "LENS: A LEO
  Satellite Network Measurement Dataset", ACM MMSys 2024).

